    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Realistic timelines and what to expect
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Recovering from dehydration takes consistency, though initial relief comes quickly once you stop stripping your skin:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Days one to three.</strong> Surface comfort improves quickly. Applying a balanced serum like the <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</a> onto damp skin eases post-wash tightness and midday sting.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks one to two.</strong> Surface texture smooths out. Flakes soften, sunscreen applies cleanly without catching, and fine dehydration lines look softer.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Weeks three to four.</strong> Barrier resilience builds. In the serum's own clinical study on 36 Indian women, ages 18 to 30, with dehydrated skin, glow increased by 35.2% at 4 weeks (results may vary). Skin retains moisture consistently through the day.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        A 10 mL bottle provides about 15 days of use to test skin tolerance, while a 30 mL bottle lasts roughly 40 days. Always patch test before first use. If severe tightness is accompanied by persistent burning, redness, or cracking, consult a dermatologist.
    </p>

    
    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can oily or acne-prone skin be dehydrated?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes. Oil and water are separate properties. Dehydrated skin often produces extra oil to compensate for missing water, creating surface shine over tight tissue. A water-based serum restores moisture without clogging pores.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Why does my face feel tight after applying hyaluronic acid?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">In dry air or air-conditioned rooms, pure hyaluronic acid pulls water upward from deeper skin layers. Applying the serum to damp skin and sealing it promptly with a moisturiser prevents this moisture from evaporating.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Should I apply a hydrating serum to wet or dry skin?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Always apply it to damp skin. Humectants bind to water molecules, so applying the serum to moist skin gives them water to hold immediately, drawing hydration into the epidermis rather than out of it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can a hydrating serum replace my daily moisturiser?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. A serum provides water and humectants, while a moisturiser supplies emollients and occlusives to seal that water in. Skipping moisturiser allows surface hydration to evaporate into the air within hours.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use a hydrating serum twice a day?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes. Using a hydrating serum morning and evening is recommended. Apply it after cleansing in the morning before moisturiser and SPF, and repeat at night to support barrier recovery while you sleep.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item" style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How can I tell if my skin is dry or dehydrated?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Dry skin is a lifelong type lacking oil. Dehydrated skin is a temporary condition lacking water, often showing fine surface crinkles, dullness, and tightness, even when the T-zone is oily.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    
